('advanced-native-1732', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1732-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["她說想按朋友真正需要給真誠支持。"],"options":["她說想按朋友真正需要給真誠支持。","她只按照片效果選工作，沒有問朋友需要。","她先決定自己喜歡做的部分，之後才問朋友擔心甚麼。","她只把協助當換取日後相同服務的條件。"]},"advanced-native-1732-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["She tried to support the person rather than make herself the centre of the move.","She wanted to help from the heart and asked what worried her friend most.","She chose the offered task from the friend’s concern rather than a photo opportunity.","Her first step was listening before deciding what to offer."],"options":["She tried to support the person rather than make herself the centre of the move.","She wanted to help from the heart and asked what worried her friend most.","She chose the offered task from the friend’s concern rather than a photo opportunity.","Her first step was listening before deciding what to offer."]},"advanced-native-1732-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["He describes wanting to help from the heart, and accepting thanks does not contradict that."],"options":["Accepting thanks proves that his stated concern could not have been sincere.","The account says he chose the help only to receive a public prize.","He describes wanting to help from the heart, and accepting thanks does not contradict that."]},"advanced-native-1732-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["只要是真心，就不能說明自己有空的時間或限制。"],"options":["只要是真心，就不能說明自己有空的時間或限制。","仍可先問對方歡迎怎樣的幫助。","出於真誠關懷提供支持。"]},"advanced-native-1732-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["To help from the heart, she can begin with what her friend actually needs, not what makes the best picture."],"options":["Let the photograph decide the task before listening to the friend’s concern.","Ask the friend to be publicly grateful before making any practical offer.","To help from the heart, she can begin with what her friend actually needs, not what makes the best picture."]},"advanced-native-1732-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["I was glad to help from the heart, and I appreciate your thanks. Could you describe the work rather than my private story, and check that short introduction with me first?","I wanted to help from the heart, not to make my personal experience part of the event. A simple acknowledgement of the task would be welcome if we agree the wording first."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1733', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1733-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["一個小行動後來反覆出現，成為接納別人的模式。"],"options":["最初行動只出現一次，此後敘述沒有任何重複。","她每次都等同學主動要求，沒有自己開始為安靜者留空間。","她後來只把發言機會留給最愛搶答的人。","一個小行動後來反覆出現，成為接納別人的模式。"]},"advanced-native-1733-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["We saw repeated action over the term, not just the first moment.","Her attention to quieter classmates began to form a pattern.","Small seeds often grow into strong habits, and she kept making room for quieter voices.","The invitation became part of how she handled later discussions."],"options":["We saw repeated action over the term, not just the first moment.","Her attention to quieter classmates began to form a pattern.","Small seeds often grow into strong habits, and she kept making room for quieter voices.","The invitation became part of how she handled later discussions."]},"advanced-native-1733-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Small seeds often grow into strong habits, as those repeated offers suggest."],"options":["The change was only a longer list of duties written by the family, with no repeated offers from the child.","Small seeds often grow into strong habits, as those repeated offers suggest.","The story describes only a promise, with no later action after the first event."]},"advanced-native-1733-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["一次小行動必定自動帶來永久不變的行為。"],"options":["需看後來怎反覆做，才可談發展。","細小行動可經重複發展成習慣。","一次小行動必定自動帶來永久不變的行為。"]},"advanced-native-1733-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Small seeds often grow into strong habits; the later pattern is why the first small step matters here."],"options":["Begin the account with the public promise and leave the earlier small invitation unexplained.","Describe the first invitation as the complete habit and ignore what happened over the term.","Small seeds often grow into strong habits; the later pattern is why the first small step matters here."]},"advanced-native-1733-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Small seeds often grow into strong habits, so I would like to note one useful phrase after a real conversation and try it in my own sentence. Could we look back at the journal together once a week?","Small seeds often grow into strong habits, and I hope this brief learning journal becomes something I return to. Let us choose one day each week to see which phrases I have actually tried using."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1734', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1734-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["反覆的小照顧，具體呈現平常關懷。"],"options":["敘述把所有公開聚會都判成不真誠表演。","每次照顧只為規定的獎項評分，沒有提實際需要。","反覆的小照顧，具體呈現平常關懷。","管理員只在周年典禮公開提及幫忙，平日沒有相關行動。"]},"advanced-native-1734-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["He remembered practical needs before each weekly meeting.","The care appeared in small repeated preparations, not only in speeches.","He checked whether people could reach a place to sit before the event began.","It was not a grand performance but a quiet habit of the heart, shown in checking chairs and access."],"options":["He remembered practical needs before each weekly meeting.","The care appeared in small repeated preparations, not only in speeches.","He checked whether people could reach a place to sit before the event began.","It was not a grand performance but a quiet habit of the heart, shown in checking chairs and access."]},"advanced-native-1734-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Her care is not a grand performance but a quiet habit of the heart."],"options":["Her care is not a grand performance but a quiet habit of the heart.","The account describes her competing publicly for credit instead of checking what the companion needs.","The repeated question is presented as a once-only formal ceremony."]},"advanced-native-1734-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["凡在公開場合出現的幫助都必定沒有真心。"],"options":["此處重視具體反覆而真誠的關懷。","凡在公開場合出現的幫助都必定沒有真心。","需看行為及情境，不只按音量大小評判。"]},"advanced-native-1734-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["The contrast is about repeated care, not a rule that public help is insincere; look at what he actually does each week."],"options":["The contrast is about repeated care, not a rule that public help is insincere; look at what he actually does each week.","Judge the help only by whether an audience could see it, without asking whom it served.","Leave out the chair checks because they happened before a public gathering."]},"advanced-native-1734-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Her care was not a grand performance but a quiet habit of the heart, including the recordings she kept for relatives far away. I would keep that detail beside the birthday celebrations so readers can see the ordinary connection too.","Her care was not a grand performance but a quiet habit of the heart, expressed in asking what distant relatives wanted to hear. I would include that repeated question in the family introduction without dismissing the parties."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1735', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1735-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["熟路與新人讀圖角度互補，兩人比較後改善圖例。"],"options":["地圖在伙伴提意見前，已因同一圖例問題修改。","熟路與新人讀圖角度互補，兩人比較後改善圖例。","伙伴只是照抄原圖，沒有提出不同看法。","兩人只比較誰較熟路，沒有討論初訪者怎讀圖。"]},"advanced-native-1735-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Two heads are often better than one; her first-reader questions added to my route knowledge.","She spotted a confusing legend that I had overlooked.","We compared local knowledge with the needs of someone new to the route.","The revision came from considering both perspectives, not merely copying one."],"options":["Two heads are often better than one; her first-reader questions added to my route knowledge.","She spotted a confusing legend that I had overlooked.","We compared local knowledge with the needs of someone new to the route.","The revision came from considering both perspectives, not merely copying one."]},"advanced-native-1735-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["Two heads are often better than one when the readers bring those different perspectives."],"options":["Two heads are often better than one when the readers bring those different perspectives.","The second reader should repeat the first view so the difference disappears before discussion.","The account says neither person made any change after hearing the other."]},"advanced-native-1735-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["只要有兩人，答案就必然正確而無需核對。"],"options":["合作思考可帶來互補想法。","只要有兩人，答案就必然正確而無需核對。","不同角度仍需比較及實際討論。"]},"advanced-native-1735-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["Two heads are often better than one because we can compare what each of us notices, not because we start with identical views."],"options":["Choose the more confident speaker’s version before hearing the other person’s reason.","Keep both versions unchanged without comparing how a visitor would read them.","Two heads are often better than one because we can compare what each of us notices, not because we start with identical views."]},"advanced-nat