('advanced-native-1760', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1760-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["可用記錄問原因及人的影響，讓資料不只被擱置。"],"options":["導師已給完整搬遷原因，無需學生再查記錄。","可用記錄問原因及人的影響，讓資料不只被擱置。","導師只叫學生抄完整目錄，沒問記錄可解甚麼問題。","導師只叫學生按目前路線推算，不需再查舊資料。"]},"advanced-native-1760-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["Use them for questions about change, rather than leave them as a dusty shelf of dead facts.","Connect the garden’s move with the routes people actually used.","Look for reasons and effects instead of only copying the catalogue.","Bring the old information into a present investigation."],"options":["Use them for questions about change, rather than leave them as a dusty shelf of dead facts.","Connect the garden’s move with the routes people actually used.","Look for reasons and effects instead of only copying the catalogue.","Bring the old information into a present investigation."]},"advanced-native-1760-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["They are not merely a dusty shelf of dead facts when students are using them to explain the changes."],"options":["The records’ age establishes that the students cannot use them to investigate a question.","The students have only copied the catalogue and have not connected any records with a question.","They are not merely a dusty shelf of dead facts when students are using them to explain the changes."]},"advanced-native-1760-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["存得較久的記錄就必沒有研究價值。"],"options":["存得較久的記錄就必沒有研究價值。","可以用新的問題重看舊資料。","批評資料沒有被用來建立理解。"]},"advanced-native-1760-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["To avoid a dusty shelf of dead facts, we need to use the records to investigate the move, not only renumber them."],"options":["Copy every entry in date order without relating any entry to the garden question.","To avoid a dusty shelf of dead facts, we need to use the records to investigate the move, not only renumber them.","Replace the archive list with a new list but keep it detached from the garden question."]},"advanced-native-1760-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Our research need not become a dusty shelf of dead facts after we hand it in. Could we make a short index of the questions, source locations and open gaps so the next group can use it?","I would like to keep the school history from becoming a dusty shelf of dead facts by leaving a guide for future students. It could show which records answer each question and where another investigation might begin."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
('advanced-native-1762', '["phrase"]'::jsonb, '{"advanced-native-1762-v1-audio":{"type":"mc","answers":["同一人作決定及評投訴，沒有獨立覆核。"],"options":["成員已能交獨立小組審查主席的決定。","主席只是按大家已通過的規則記錄出席。","主席沒作任何決定，權力完全未被使用。","同一人作決定及評投訴，沒有獨立覆核。"]},"advanced-native-1762-v2-reply":{"type":"mc","answers":["The same person controlled both the rule change and its review.","The members could not ask another body to examine what he had done.","Power went unchecked because he judged complaints about the rules he alone had changed.","There was no independent route for members to question the decisions."],"options":["The same person controlled both the rule change and its review.","The members could not ask another body to examine what he had done.","Power went unchecked because he judged complaints about the rules he alone had changed.","There was no independent route for members to question the decisions."]},"advanced-native-1762-v1-scene":{"type":"mc","answers":["An unpopular result does not show that power goes unchecked when independent review has actually changed part of the decision."],"options":["The original committee retained sole control of the appeal and left every part of its decision unchanged.","An unpopular result does not show that power goes unchecked when independent review has actually changed part of the decision.","The remaining dissatisfaction is enough to describe the authority as lacking independent review."]},"advanced-native-1762-v1-contrast":{"type":"mc","answers":["決定有理由記錄，另有可實際質疑及覆核的獨立途徑。"],"options":["受影響的人沒有可用方式審查掌權者決定。","負責人自己定規則，也可拒絕讓別人覆核。","決定有理由記錄，另有可實際質疑及覆核的獨立途徑。"]},"advanced-native-1762-v1-branch":{"type":"mc","answers":["We need to ask who can review the decisions before saying power goes unchecked; a title alone does not answer that."],"options":["Count how often the chair speaks instead of asking whether decisions can be challenged.","We need to ask who can review the decisions before saying power goes unchecked; a title alone does not answer that.","Judge oversight only from the chair’s title, without looking at the appeal process."]},"advanced-native-1762-v1-final":{"type":"open","answers":["Could we compare what happens when power goes unchecked with what happens when the council can question a leader? I would like to trace how that difference shapes the characters’ choices, rather than judge them only by their speeches.","In one story, power goes unchecked because the leader can dismiss complaints about his own actions. Let us compare that arrangement with the other novel’s council and ask what each character is allowed to challenge."],"options":[]}}'::jsonb),
